course: dictionary
lesson: 1858
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them show you which meaning the writer means. The word coffee is a good example: it can be a drink, the beans, a cup, or even a colour. «Many grown-ups drink things that change how they feel: coffee and tea wake them up.» Here coffee is the hot drink, because you drink things that wake you up.
explain: «Example: in a café in Toronto, Mum taps her phone on the reader and the coffee is paid in a second.» The coffee is something you pay for in a café, so it means the drink, or a cup of it. Ask yourself what would make sense in the sentence, then try that meaning in place of the word.
explain: «Connor looks both up: a toque is a woolly hat, a double-double is coffee with two creams and two sugars.» Connor's words are not hard to crack. A double-double is a drink, and the clues creams and sugars tell you what kind of coffee it is.
fact: Coffee is a hot, dark-brown drink made from roasted, ground beans.
fact: The beans are the seeds of the coffee plant, which grows in hot countries like Brazil, Colombia, Ethiopia and Vietnam.
fact: «A coffee» means one cup of the drink, and coffees means more than one cup.
fact: Coffee can also mean a light brown colour.
fact: Coffee has caffeine, which keeps you awake. It is not good for children, and hot coffee can scald, so keep hot drinks away from table edges and babies.
exercise: «Many grown-ups drink things that change how they feel: coffee and tea wake them up.» What does coffee do here? | Makes people grow taller | *Wakes people up | Makes people sleepy | Keeps people warm in bed
exercise: A double-double is coffee with two creams and two sugars. What is a double-double? | *A coffee drink with milk and sugar | A type of tea with lemon | A woolly hat | A low table in a living room
exercise: In «the coffee is paid in a second», what does coffee mean? | A woolly hat | A light brown colour | A low table in a living room | *A cup of the drink
test: In «Apples, almonds, strawberries and coffee all need pollinators», which word is a drink? | Apples | Strawberries | *Coffee | Almonds
test: What does coffee mean in «a coffee-coloured rug»? | A coffee bean | A hot drink | A cup of tea | *A light brown colour
exam: Why must hot coffee be kept away from table edges and babies? | *It can scald | It is too sweet | It is only for grown-ups | It keeps you awake
